For CALVIN,
  the usual path is to download the official CALVIN dataset, especially the ABC_D split that X-VLA reports using.

  Use this on Palmetto:

  cd /scratch/shahils/openpi/third_party

  git clone --recurse-submodules https://github.com/mees/calvin.git

  export CALVIN_ROOT=/scratch/shahils/openpi/third_party/calvin
  cd $CALVIN_ROOT/dataset

  # X-VLA Calvin checkpoint is trained on ABC_D, so use ABC
  sh download_data.sh ABC

  That should create something like:

  /scratch/shahils/openpi/third_party/calvin/dataset/task_ABC_D/
    training/
    validation/

  If you only want a tiny test download first:

  cd /scratch/shahils/openpi/third_party/calvin/dataset
  sh download_data.sh debug

  Important: official CALVIN notes that older ABC/ABCD downloads had annotation and scene_info.npy fixes. If your downloaded script is current, it may already handle this, but if not, run:

  cd /scratch/shahils/openpi/third_party/calvin/dataset/task_ABC_D

  wget http://calvin.cs.uni-freiburg.de/scene_info_fix/task_ABC_D_scene_info.zip
  unzip -o task_ABC_D_scene_info.zip
  rm task_ABC_D_scene_info.zip

  For X-VLA training, downloading CALVIN is only step 1. You still need either:

  official CALVIN episodes -> X-VLA-compatible trajectory files -> meta JSON

  or a custom X-VLA domain handler that reads CALVIN’s native episode format directly.

  The expected X-VLA training command will eventually look like:

  accelerate launch \
    --mixed_precision bf16 \
    train.py \
    --models 2toINF/X-VLA-Pt \
    --train_metas_path /scratch/shahils/openpi/datasets/calvin_abc_d_xvla/meta.json \
    --learning_rate 1e-4 \
    --learning_coef 0.1 \
    --iters 50000 \
    --freeze_steps 1000 \
    --warmup_steps 2000

  So: yes, download is straightforward with CALVIN’s official script, but unlike LIBERO I would not assume there is a ready-made X-VLA-format dataset unless you find one in the X-VLA issues. The split you
  want for their Calvin model is ABC, producing task_ABC_D.

  Sources: CALVIN official repo download instructions and X-VLA README/model listing for X-VLA-Calvin-ABC_D.

